  "lists": [
    "blind-75",
    "grind-75",
    "interview-150"
  ],
  "hints": [
    "any coin can be reused any number of times, and you're minimizing a count - what's the smallest subproblem you can define, in terms of a smaller remaining amount?",
    "define dp[a] as the fewest coins needed to make exactly amount a, with dp[0] = 0",
    "for a given a, try using each coin c as the last coin placed: dp[a] = 1 + dp[a - c], but only if a - c >= 0 and dp[a - c] is reachable",
    "dp[a] is the minimum of that expression over every coin c that fits, or 'unreachable' if none of them lead anywhere",
    "use a sentinel like infinity (or amount + 1) to mark unreachable amounts, build dp up from 0 to amount, and convert the sentinel to -1 only at the very end"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "returning 0 or -1 too early instead of properly propagating 'unreachable' through the DP as a large sentinel value",
    "checking amount == 0 only at the top level instead of handling dp[0] = 0 as a real base case inside the table",
    "off-by-one on the loop bound, never considering a coin exactly equal to the remaining amount"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given a list of coin denominations, `coins`, and a target `amount`.\nEach denomination is available in unlimited supply.\n\n**Return the fewest number of coins needed to make exactly that amount.**\n\nIf it's impossible to make the amount with the given coins, return -1.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "1 <= coins.length <= 12",
      "1 <= coins[i] <= 2^31 - 1",
      "0 <= amount <= 10^4"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "amount is 0 (always 0 coins needed)",
      "amount cannot be formed by any combination of coins (return -1)",
      "a coin denomination equal to the amount itself"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "coins = [1, 2, 5], amount = 11",
        "output": "3",
        "expectedOutput": "3",
        "explanation": "11 = 5 + 5 + 1, using 3 coins"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_2",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "coins = [2], amount = 3",
        "output": "-1",
        "expectedOutput": "-1",
        "explanation": "only even amounts are reachable with a single coin of value 2"
      },
      {
        "id": "sample_3",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "coins = [1], amount = 0",
        "output": "0",
        "expectedOutput": "0",
        "explanation": "zero coins are needed to make an amount of 0"
      }
    ],
